runs it; putting ads in or around it; offering it as part of a paid
product or service; and using it inside a business to make money.


2. What you may do

As long as you follow this license and do not make commercial use of
the software, you may:

  (a) Use it. Download it, run it, and use every part of it. That
      includes running your own relay and run server, for yourself and
      for the people you choose to let in, and using a server that
      someone else runs.

  (b) Change it for yourself. Make changes and run the changed version
      on your own computers and servers, and let the people you choose
      use your server while it runs that version.

  (c) Contribute. Fork the official repository on GitHub, make changes
      in that fork, and offer them back as pull requests. Your fork
      must stay a GitHub fork of the official repository.

  (d) Pass on a release file. Give an unchanged official release file
      (for example OUTPOST-STANDALONE.html) to someone, privately and
      free of charge, for their own use under this license.

  (e) Point people to it. Link to the official repository, its
      releases, or a server running the software.


3. What you may not do

  (a) Make commercial use of the software.

  (b) Redistribute it. Do not publish, upload, mirror or hand out the
      software, a changed version of it, or a substantial part of it,
      anywhere other than as allowed in 2(c) and 2(d). That covers
      other Git repositories (on GitHub or anywhere else), other code
      hosts, package registries, app and extension stores, download and
      file-sharing sites, and bundles with other software. Running the
      software on your server so people can use it is not
      redistribution; handing out its files is.

  (c) Remove or change the copyright notice, this license, or the
      credit to the licensor in the software.

  (d) Present a server you run, or a changed version you make, as the
      official one.

  (e) Sublicense the software, or grant anyone more rights in it than
      this license gives you.


4. Your contributions

When you send a pull request, a patch or any other contribution to
